  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In general, the temperature of the system may change during a process. If the process is reversible, the change in entropy is defined as<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br />In an adiabatic reversible process, no heat is given to the system. Therefore, entropy of the system remains constant.&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
